<article class="env-lemma" id="0EDB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EDB">Lemma <span data-tag="0EDB">72.15.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be an integral morphism of algebraic spaces. Then $\dim (X) \leq \dim (Y)$. If $f$ is surjective then $\dim (X) = \dim (Y)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $V \to Y$ surjective étale with $V$ a scheme. Then $U = X \times _ Y V$ is a scheme and $U \to V$ is integral (and surjective if $f$ is surjective). By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A4H" data-tag="0A4H">66.22.5</a> we have $\dim (X) = \dim (U)$ and $\dim (Y) = \dim (V)$. Thus the result follows from the case of schemes which is Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ECG" data-tag="0ECG">29.45.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>